        "original_id": "08140139-190e-51e5-97c7-2a35b0bfe2af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Animals: birds, ostrich, bee hummingbird\n- Places: worldwide, Africa\n- Taxonomy: Struthio camelus, Struthio, ratites\n\nFacts:\n- Birds live worldwide.\n- Birds range in size from the 5 cm bee hummingbird to the 2.75 m ostrich.\n- The ostrich, or common ostrich, is named Struthio camelus.\n- The common ostrich is native to Africa.\n- The common ostrich is a large flightless bird.\n- The common ostrich is the only living member of the genus Struthio.\n- The genus Struthio belongs to the ratite family.\n- Sources differ on whether the ostrich is one species or two species.",
